{
  "_comment": "Artifact-type registry for the Visual Studio workflow. Downloaded through DownloadTemplate (template_name: datasets/visual_types.json) with an empty template_vars, so this file must contain no doubled-curly-brace placeholder anywhere, not even in a comment. It declares how each type is authored, rendered and formatted; the workflow routes on these fields and adding a type is a data change. Raster art direction is NOT here: it stays in datasets/image_motifs.json, and the raster prompt only receives the spec this registry's authoring stage produces.",
  "_comment_author": "author is one of: raster (content -> image prompt -> image model), spec_raster (content -> content spec -> raster prompt -> image model), spec_markup (content -> content spec -> deterministic markup from template), spec_service (content spec -> render service -> mp4), agent (content -> the pi-render agent authors and renders a composition -> the artifact).",
  "_comment_render": "render is one of: static (one raster file), animated (browser frame capture -> img2webp animated webp, gif fallback via GraphicsMagick), text (authored markup committed as-is, never rasterized), video (the render service composes and encodes an mp4).",
  "_comment_budget": "budget.fps/frames/viewport are the animation ceiling. A type may override them lower; the renderer never exceeds the registry value. 12 fps, 36 frames (3 s), 1200 px viewport.",
  "_comment_default": "Requested types come from the caller's ASSET_TYPES parameter (comma-separated). When it is blank, default_types is used. max_types_per_request caps one request.",
